WHY
The Rent tab renders payments and expenses as flat lists. Grouping them by financial
year is presentation, but deciding WHICH year a date belongs to is domain logic, so it
lives in lib/ where it is testable rather than inside a component.

Three decisions worth recording:
1. The year is derived by reusing currentFyEndYear from ./fy rather than writing new
   calendar arithmetic. There is exactly one definition of a financial-year boundary in
   this codebase and this module does not become a second one.
2. Dates parse as UTC via an explicit Z, per the rationale at the top of ./fy. Confirmed
   empirically before writing the test: with TZ=Australia/Sydney,
   new Date(2025,6,1).toISOString() is '2025-06-30T14:00:00.000Z', which would file
   1 July under the previous financial year.
3. Rows with a missing or unreadable date go to a trailing 'Undated' group instead of
   being dropped. A dropped row would make the per-year subtotals disagree with the
   lifetime total displayed in the same card.

fyEndYearForDate also accepts a full ISO timestamp by taking the leading UTC calendar
day, so a column that later gains a time component does not silently report every row
as undated.

